  "id": "COMPOUND:24022 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Miyabenol A is shown to have a target relationship with VMRC-MELG through multiple pathways, with Ataxin-2 and 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 acting as intermediate targets. These targets are all linked to VMRC-MELG via a complex, multi-step biochemical pathway involving a specific metabolite, (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one. This metabolite is a known target of several compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, which in turn is linked to VMRC-MELG. The evidence suggests that Miyabenol A may act through a mechanism that involves the metabolism of this compound, leading to its interaction with VMRC-MELG. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Miyabenol A in modulating the activity of VMRC-MELG through a complex, multi-targeted biochemical process.",
